var a = "global";
{
  fun showA() {
    print a;
  }

  showA();
  var a = "block";
  showA();
}

// Should print "global" twice
/*
The first call to showA() should definitely print “global” since we haven’t even reached the declaration of the inner a yet. And by our rule that a variable expression always resolves to the same variable, that implies the second call to showA() should print the same thing.
*/
